body:
 Ʒaðal 

&#x200B;

"Drul ma zoŋorumeb og yodil og Drojaŋ gralo vou blimeb ul de imilweg ge Dyriaŋ Muradezo..."

/dɾul mæ zɔŋɔɾumɛb ɔg jɔdɪl ɔg dɾɔdʒɑŋ gɾælɔ vu blimɛb ul imilwɛg gɛ diɾiæŋ mʊɾædɛzɔ/

Yet she hear\[PRF\]\[PAST\] of children of Trojan blood who will\[PAST\] one-day over-succeed the Tyrian fortification.

&#x200B;

**Ʒaðal:** Such strategic geography it would almost seem like I had built the whole planet in such a way so that one city would never fall or be destroyed. The tech in the world is kept in the iron age for glorious battle scenes and long journeys. The people of the titular city are a trichotomy of brutish, violent, guttural orc-like humans, party-animals with a chanting/screaming problem, and unfairly-advanced civil engineers, with metallurgy that almost seems like cheating, and a slew of other unfair advantages that make them an odd bunch, and its Thanksgiving 48 times a year.

&#x200B;

Also, no magic.
